Before opening a layout, start Magic from this directory without naming a
layout file.  For example, from a shell:

    cd /foss/designs/sg13cmos5l_ocd_openframe/magic
    magic

Then source the setup script at the Magic Tcl prompt (not from the shell):

    source ../scripts/layout_setup.tcl

This resolves the paths to the dependent cell libraries.  After sourcing the
script, open the desired layout with Magic's `load` command.  For example:

    load <cell-name>

The setup script can be sourced later, but sourcing it before loading a layout
prevents warnings about cells that Magic cannot find.
